  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A girl counts on her fingers by counting 1 on her thumb, 2 on her index finger, 3 on her middle\nfinger, 4 on her ring finger, and 5 on her little finger. Then she continues the other way, counting 6\non her ring finger, 7 on her middle finger, 8 on her index finger, and 9 on her thumb. Then she\ncontinues the other way, counting 10 on her index finger, 11 on her middle finger, 12 on her ring\nfinger, and 13 on her little finger. She continues in this way indefinitely as shown in the image\nbelow:\n\n![image](https://s3.amazonaws.com/hr-assets/0/1751976253-9789b30239-Countnumbers.png)\n\nYou are given a function,\nint CountingOnFingers(int n);\nint CountingOnFingers(int n);\nstatic int CountingOnFingers(int n){}\nstatic int CountingOnFingers(int n){}\ndef CountingOnFingers(n):\nThe function takes a number 'n' as input and returns which finger the girl will be on when her count\nreaches 'n'. Assume 'n' >= 1. If she will be on her thumb, then return 1, if index finger then return\n2, if middle finger then return 3, if ring finger then return 4 and if little finger then return 5.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
